vity reflected in EEG coherence in individuals with autism.</article-title><source>Biol Psychiatry</source><volume>62</volume><fpage>270</fpage><lpage>273</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17336944</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000334-Folstein1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Folstein</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Twin and adoption studies in child and adolescent psychiatric disorders.</article-title><source>Curr Opin Pediatr</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>339</fpage><lpage>347</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8954264</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000334-Panksepp1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Panksepp</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><source>Affective neuroscience: The foundations of human and animal emotions</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000334-Breiter1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Breiter</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Gasic</surname><given-names>GP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>A general circuitry processing reward/aversion information and its implications for neuropsychiatric illness.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Gazzaniga</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Cognitive Neurosciences III</source><publisher-loc>Cambridge</publisher-loc><publisher-name>MIT Press</publisher-name><fpage>1043</fpage><lpage>1065</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000334-Panksepp2"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Panksepp</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Emotional endophenotypes in evolutionary psychiatry.</article-title><source>Prog Neuropsychopharmacol Biol Psychiatry</source><volume>30</volume><fpage>774</fpage><lpage>784</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16554114</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000334-Gustafson1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gustafson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bug</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Nissanov</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>NeuroTerrain&#x02014;a client-server system for browsing 3D biomedical image data sets.</article-title><source>BMC Bioinformatics</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>40</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17280615</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000334-MacKenzieGraham1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>MacKenzie-Graham</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Shattuck</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Dinov</surname><given-names>ID</given-names></name><name><surname>Bota</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>The informatics of a C57BL/6J mouse brain atlas.</article-title><source>Neuroinformatics</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>397</fpage><lpage>410</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15043223</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000334-Visel1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Visel</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Thaller</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Eichele</surname><given-names>G</given-names></